  "notes": "The minimal-repetition end of the charting SoundCloud wave — four-word hooks over two-element beats. The distinguishing parameters are all documented: **\"booming drums\"** mixed to clip, **one long-decay 808 per chord tuned to the tonic** and pushed until the transient distorts, and **\"a hazy piano melody\"** — one 2-bar low-pass-filtered keyboard figure with no pad and no countermelody. Unusually often *major* despite the aggressive framing. ⚠ `medium`: tempo, key and instrumentation are individually sourced; the drum-placement specifics are less so. ⚠ **The countermelody reached 966/1000 distinct answers against a floor of 980**, so its style pool was opened: bell_echo, arp, densityRatio 0.55. ⛔ `counter.rs` reads five styles and this roster only ever authored three — `bell_echo` is a real answer shape the engine can already play and the dataset had never asked for. ⚠ `sustain_pad` is deliberately not added: it is a held pad rather than an answer, and adding one to win a variety score would change what the record sounds like.",
